  "term": "high blood pressure",
  "definition": "High blood pressure, or hypertension, is a condition in which the pressure in the arteries is higher than normal. In the source, it is described as a systolic pressure of 140 mmHg or more, a diastolic pressure of 90 mmHg or more, or a self-reported case being treated with medication, and it is linked to increased risk of heart, stroke, and kidney problems.",
